null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv115glnkpof"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628354661,"type":"mcq","q":"All pure substances have:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"the same physical state","img":null},{"t":"Same colour","img":null},{"t":"Same composition","img":null},{"t":"Definite sets of properties","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"All pure substances have a definite set of properties. These properties include physical state, colour and composition, but they are not the same for all substances.\nPure substances can exist in different states - solid, liquid or gas. Different pure substances have different colours. Each pure substance has a fixed composition, but it is not the same as that of other substances.","expImg":null,"id":"mv299i06csl8"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628483129,"type":"mcq","q":"Sugar is a compound which consists of the elements:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"C and H","img":null},{"t":"H and O","img":null},{"t":"C , H, O","img":null},{"t":"Hydrogen, Carbon, Sulphur","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":"content/media/6a6bccb976339634.jpg","id":"mv29c99dqi6f"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628626505,"type":"mcq","q":"Sulphur and Carbon are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Metal","img":null},{"t":"Non metals","img":null},{"t":"Metalloids","img":null},{"t":"Mentals","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"Sulphur and carbon are non-metals with dull surfaces that do not shine unlike metals being lustrous. \nSulphur and carbon do not show metallic properties like conductivity or malleability. Metalloids have properties of both metals and non-metals (e.g., silicon). Noble gases (like helium, neon) are inert gases, unlike sulphur and carbon.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29fbrdloeo"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628883441,"type":"mcq","q":"The most abundant elements in the universe are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Neon and argon","img":null},{"t":"Hydrogen and helium","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium and copper","img":null},{"t":"Oxygen and nitrogen","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29ku0j7ygq"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628936522,"type":"mcq","q":"The symbol of which of the following elements is derived from its Latin name ?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Cobult","img":null},{"t":"Copper","img":null},{"t":"Calcium","img":null},{"t":"Chlorine","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"Among the following elements the symbol of copper i.e., Cu is derived from its latin name \"Cuprum\".","expImg":null,"id":"mv29lyyy1j3c"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791628993622,"type":"mcq","q":"The metal which is not a good conductor of electricity is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Silver","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium","img":null},{"t":"Tungsten","img":null},{"t":"Copper","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"Metals are good conductors of electricity excepting tungsten, which is a poor conductor of electricity.\nSilver is the best conductor of electricity. Aluminium is a good conductor and commonly used in power cables. Copper is a very good conductor, widely used in wiring.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29n712zetn"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629017886,"type":"mcq","q":"Symbol of sodium","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"S","img":null},{"t":"N","img":null},{"t":"Na","img":null},{"t":"Sn","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29npr31kr3"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629185038,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/3bcc464e212621cc.jpg","opts":[{"t":"(a)-(3), (b)-(4), (c)-(2), (d)-(5), (e)-(1)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(3), (b)-(2), (c)-(4), (d)-(1), (e)-(5)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(5), (b)-(4), (c)-(2), (d)-(3), (e)-(1)","img":null},{"t":"(a)-(1), (b)-(3), (c)-(5), (d)-(2), (e)-(4)","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29raw87vkr"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629380450,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/a8a615e86164fb4f.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","img":null},{"t":"Both A and R are true and R is not the correct explanation of A.","img":null},{"t":"A true B false","img":null},{"t":"A false B true","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29vhn4kz69"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629443386,"type":"mcq","q":"Brass and Bronze are","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Elements","img":null},{"t":"Compound","img":null},{"t":"Mixture","img":null},{"t":"None of these","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"Brass is a mixture of copper and zinc and bronze is a mixture of copper and tin.\nBrass and bronze are not single elements; they are made of more than one metal. So, they can't be elements. Compounds have a fixed chemical formula, but alloys do not.","expImg":null,"id":"mv29wu2izzio"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629473358,"type":"mcq","q":"The hardest naturally occurring substance is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Graphite","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null},{"t":"Diamond","img":null},{"t":"Coal","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29xh73zaxw"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629516086,"type":"mcq","q":"Gold is used to make jewellery because it is","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Dull","img":null},{"t":"Malleable","img":null},{"t":"Ductile","img":null},{"t":"Lustrous and attractive","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29ye5z839y"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629567629,"type":"mcq","q":"A liquid non metal is","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Carbon","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null},{"t":"Bromine","img":null},{"t":"Boron","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv29zhxp8gnt"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629772893,"type":"mcq","q":"A mixture of mustard oil and water forms:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Compound","img":null},{"t":"An alloy","img":null},{"t":"Homogeneous mixture","img":null},{"t":"Heterogeneous mixture","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"Mustard oil and water are immiscible liquids. Their mixture is not uniformly distributed throughout. Hence, they form a heterogeneous mixture.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a3wbi2gj2"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629836753,"type":"mcq","q":"A heterogeneous mixture is:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Made up of only one kind of atoms","img":null},{"t":"made up of only one kind of molecules","img":null},{"t":"made up of different kinds of atoms and molecules.","img":null},{"t":"one that looks uniform.","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a59ldbixj"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629871018,"type":"mcq","q":"An example of a homogeneous mixture is :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Distilled water","img":null},{"t":"Sand water","img":null},{"t":"Sawdust and water","img":null},{"t":"Tap water","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a60173uea"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629920306,"type":"mcq","q":"Which among the following is a set containing only mixtures ?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"gold, common salt, water, alloy","img":null},{"t":"alloy, ink, honey, ice-cream","img":null},{"t":"milk, duralumin, brass, silver.","img":null},{"t":"alloy, mercury, air, sea water","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a722asngi"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629951207,"type":"mcq","q":"Copper is not a part of the alloy :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"steel","img":null},{"t":"Brass","img":null},{"t":"Bronze","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a7pwn6fn1"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791629989507,"type":"mcq","q":"Which of the following is not a mixture or impure substances?","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Distilled water","img":null},{"t":"Sugar solution","img":null},{"t":"Tap water","img":null},{"t":"Milk","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2a8jgk5wwq"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630068339,"type":"mcq","q":"Alloys are which type of mixture","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Solid liquid","img":null},{"t":"Liquid liquid","img":null},{"t":"Solid gas","img":null},{"t":"Solid solid","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2aa8ac6t18"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630135826,"type":"mcq","q":"The process of adding a chemical substance to help the suspended solid particles to deposit as sediment faster is called:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Sedimentation","img":null},{"t":"Loading","img":null},{"t":"Decantation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"The process of helping fine solid particles in a solid-liquid mixture to settle faster, by adding a special chemical, is called loading or coagulation.\nSedimentation is the natural settling of particles at the bottom without adding any chemical. Decantation is the process of carefully pouring off the clear liquid after sedimentation. Filtration is the process of separating solids from liquids using a filter.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2abocy9uey"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630171488,"type":"mcq","q":"Salt is separated from sea water by:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Evaporation","img":null},{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Magnetic separation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2acfvl1jeu"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630219556,"type":"mcq","q":"A gas dissolved in a liquid can be separated by:","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Filtration","img":null},{"t":"Using magnet","img":null},{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Boiling","img":null}],"ans":3,"exp":"A mixture of gas in liquid can be separated by heating or boiling. Dissolved gas escapes from the liquid on heating or boiling.\nFiltration is used to separate insoluble solids from liquids, not dissolved gases. Magnet works only for magnetic materials like iron. Sublimation is used for solids that directly convert into gas, not for dissolved gases.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2adgyscw10"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630260211,"type":"mcq","q":"Camphor can be separated from a mixture of sand and camphor by :","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Sublimation","img":null},{"t":"Filtration","img":null},{"t":"Winnowing","img":null},{"t":"Evaporation","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"Winnowing is used to separate lighter and heavier solids using air (like husk and grains), not suitable here.","expImg":null,"id":"mv2aecc3kiuy"},{"test":"mv297fn43q5w","n":1791630313585,"type":"mcq","q":"A separating funnel is used to separate","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"Immiscible liquid","img":null},{"t":"Miscible liquid","img":null},{"t":"Sugar solution","img":null},{"t":"Chalk powder and water","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2afhipfm8w"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791658948683,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/8d6c23d9014c10c9.jpg","opts":[{"t":"a)","img":null},{"t":"b)","img":null},{"t":"c)","img":null},{"t":"d)","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rh8pivb9h"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791659062534,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/fe336b0297c6ebcb.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rjoilxces"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791659139873,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/2897bdf7177eb955.jpg","opts":[{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null},{"t":"is right","img":null},{"t":"Is right","img":null}],"ans":2,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rlc5i8l6a"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791659336528,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/22ec15a18aed3b65.jpg","opts":[{"t":"⅙","img":null},{"t":"⅘","img":null},{"t":"⅔","img":null},{"t":"⅓","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rpjwmjhop"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791659392599,"type":"mcq","q":"If sinA+sin²A=1 then find the value of cos²A+cos⁴A","qImg":null,"opts":[{"t":"1","img":null},{"t":"2","img":null},{"t":"0","img":null},{"t":"½","img":null}],"ans":0,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rqr1353gk"},{"test":"mv2rcmv9r8iw","n":1791659469248,"type":"mcq","q":"","qImg":"content/media/1832ffb4a5a3b8ac.jpg","opts":[{"t":"0","img":null},{"t":"3","img":null},{"t":"5","img":null},{"t":"9","img":null}],"ans":1,"exp":"","expImg":null,"id":"mv2rseag29wr"},{"test":"mv2sjrp8f7qr","n":1791660992948,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Find the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial $(4u^2 + 8u$).","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"2,4","img":null},{"t":"0,-2","img":null},{"t":"0,2","img":null},{"t":"2,-4","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv2sp1vcu1gm"},{"test":"mv2sjrp8f7qr","n":1791661425044,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Find the zeroes of the quadratic polynomial \\(t^2 - 15\\).","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"15,-15","img":null},{"t":"\\(\\sqrt{5}, -\\sqrt{5}\\)","img":null},{"t":"\\(\\sqrt{15}, -\\sqrt{15}\\)","img":null},{"t":"\\(3\\sqrt{5}, -3\\sqrt{5}\\)","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv2syb9x46z5"},{"test":"mv2sjrp8f7qr","n":1791661563566,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Find a quadratic polynomial with the sum and product of its zeroes as \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) and \\(-1\\) respectively.","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"4x²-x-4","img":null},{"t":"4x²+x-4","img":null},{"t":"4x²-x+4","img":null},{"t":"x²-x+4","img":null}],"ans":0,"id":"mv2t1a5ri9tn"},{"test":"mv2sjrp8f7qr","n":1791661719865,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Find a quadratic polynomial with the sum and product of its zeroes as \\(\\sqrt{2}\\) and \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\) respectively.","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"\\(x^2 - 3\\sqrt{2}x + 3\\)","img":null},{"t":"\\(3x^2 + 3\\sqrt{2}x + 1\\)","img":null},{"t":"\\(\\sqrt{3}x^2 - 3\\sqrt{2}x + 1\\)","img":null},{"t":"D) \\(3x^2 - 3\\sqrt{2}x + 1\\)","img":null}],"ans":3,"id":"mv2t4mrdef3q"},{"test":"mv2sjrp8f7qr","n":1791661843036,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Find a quadratic polynomial with the sum and product of its zeroes as \\(0\\) and \\(\\sqrt{5}\\) respectively.","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"\\(\\sqrt{5}x^2 + 1\\)","img":null},{"t":"\\(x^2 - \\sqrt{5}\\)","img":null},{"t":"x²+5","img":null},{"t":"x²-5","img":null}],"ans":0,"id":"mv2t79st0427"},{"test":"mv3cjujatngt","n":1791694431244,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Lime water turns cloudy in the presence of a gas which is a by-product of respiration.\nShown below are four setups kept in sunlight for 24 hours.\n\nIn which setup is lime water expected to be the cloudiest?","qImg":"content/media/ae97b9dd428c99b5.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"P set","img":null},{"t":"Q set","img":null},{"t":"R set","img":null},{"t":"S set","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3clr6bk2u5"},{"test":"mv3cjujatngt","n":1791694554890,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"During photosynthesis, what happens to carbon dioxide and water as glucose is formed?","qImg":null,"exp":"• Carbon dioxide (\\(CO_{2}\\)) is reduced because it gains hydrogen atoms to form glucose (\\(C_6H_{12}O_6\\)).\n• Water (\\(H_{2}O\\)) is oxidized because it loses electrons and hydrogen ions to release oxygen gas (\\(O_{2}\\)).","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Carbon dioxide gains hydrogen, while water loses electrons.","img":null},{"t":"Carbon dioxide loses oxygen, while water gains oxygen.","img":null},{"t":"Carbon dioxide is oxidised, while water is reduced.","img":null},{"t":"Both carbon dioxide and water undergo reduction","img":null}],"ans":0,"id":"mv3coefft22i"},{"test":"mv3cjujatngt","n":1791695043159,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"From the given picture of digestive system. Identify pancreas","qImg":"content/media/cc64830b09750372.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"A","img":null},{"t":"B","img":null},{"t":"C","img":null},{"t":"D","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3cyvdp3xa0"},{"test":"mv3cjujatngt","n":1791695202993,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"","qImg":"content/media/f3beecfe0ebf49a3.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Capturing food takes time","img":null},{"t":"Complex food digested easily","img":null},{"t":"Fast distribution of nutrition within body","img":null},{"t":"More food can be consumed","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3d2an8pc4z"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791698976257,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Metal P cannot displace Q, but Q can displace R. R can displace S. Which statement is definitely true?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"P is more reactive than Q","img":null},{"t":"Q is more reactive than R","img":null},{"t":"S is more reactive than R","img":null},{"t":"P is necessarily less reactive than S","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3fb5z8ilcm"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699050967,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Why can carbon reduce ZnO but cannot normally reduce Na₂O?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Sodium oxide has no oxygen","img":null},{"t":"Sodium is less reactive than carbon","img":null},{"t":"Sodium has a greater affinity for oxygen than carbon","img":null},{"t":"Carbon reacts only with sulphides","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3fcrmgyy69"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699114423,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Which pair contains metals that generally require electrolytic methods for extraction?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Na and K","img":null},{"t":"Zn and Fe","img":null},{"t":"Cu and Hg","img":null},{"t":"Fe and Cu","img":null}],"ans":0,"id":"mv3fe4l46eol"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699171724,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Black copper(II) oxide is heated with hydrogen: \nCuO + H₂ → Cu + H₂O \nWhich substance undergoes reduction?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"H₂","img":null},{"t":"CuO","img":null},{"t":"H₂O","img":null},{"t":"Cu","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3ffcstlcpw"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699229893,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"A metal oxide MO reacts with hydrochloric acid: \nMO + 2HCl → MCl₂ + H₂O \nIf MO also reacts with sodium hydroxide, MO is most likely:","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Na₂O","img":null},{"t":"MgO","img":null},{"t":"ZnO","img":null},{"t":"CO₂","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3fglolv3pj"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699290254,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"A student performs:\n\nI. Zn + FeSO₄ → reaction \nII. Fe + CuSO₄ → reaction \nIII. Cu + ZnSO₄ → no reaction\n\nWhich order is supported?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Zn > Fe > Cu","img":null},{"t":"Cu > Fe > Zn","img":null},{"t":"Fe > Zn > Cu","img":null},{"t":"Zn > Cu > Fe","img":null}],"ans":0,"id":"mv3fhw9gv7u8"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699364917,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"The following representation shows a metal ion gaining an electron to form a metal atom.","qImg":"content/media/2cac2c8ed780541c.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"oxidation","img":null},{"t":"reduction","img":null},{"t":"corrosion","img":null},{"t":"combustion","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3fji09e1uw"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699437198,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Assertion: Ionic compounds conduct electricity in the solid state.\n\nReason: Ionic compounds contain charged particles.","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true, and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).","img":null},{"t":"Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true, but Reason (R) is not the correct explanation of Assertion (A).","img":null},{"t":"Assertion (A) is true, but Reason (R) is false.","img":null},{"t":"Assertion (A) is false, but Reason (R) is true.","img":null}],"ans":3,"id":"mv3fl1n2e5lw"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699515945,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"A copper strip is placed separately into solutions of ZnSO₄, FeSO₄ and AgNO₃. In which solution(s) will a reaction occur?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"ZnSO₄ only","img":null},{"t":"only  FeSO₄","img":null},{"t":"only  AgNO₃","img":null},{"t":"ZnSO₄ and FeSO₄","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3fmqeheaqm"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699580507,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"A student observes that aluminium does not appear to react readily with water, although aluminium is above hydrogen in the reactivity series. The best explanation is:","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Aluminium is below hydrogen in the reactivity series.","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium cannot react with oxygen.","img":null},{"t":"A protective oxide layer forms on aluminium.","img":null},{"t":"Aluminium reacts only with acids.","img":null}],"ans":2,"id":"mv3fo47vl89u"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699669749,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Why does the mass of the anode decrease during the electrolytic refining of copper?","qImg":"content/media/0079bb60f600beea.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Copper ions from the electrolyte get deposited on the anode.","img":null},{"t":"Copper atoms from the anode lose electrons and enter the electrolyte as Cu²⁺ ions.","img":null},{"t":"The anode dissolves because water molecules attack it.","img":null},{"t":"Copper ions from the electrolyte react with impurities at the anode.","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3fq18ev45z"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699737332,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"The following experiment is used to compare the thermal conductivity of four metal rods A, B, C and D. The rods have equal length and thickness and are heated equally at one end. Wax pins are attached at equal distances from the heated end.\n\nWhich of the following represents the correct decreasing order of thermal conductivity?","qImg":"content/media/e64b5bfcd5fc4baa.jpg","exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"D > C > B > A","img":null},{"t":"A > B > C > D","img":null},{"t":"B > A > D > C","img":null},{"t":"A > C > B > D","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3frhcud6bm"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699806476,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"An ionic compound X has a high melting point and is soluble in water. Which observation is most likely?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Solid X conducts electricity strongly.","img":null},{"t":"Molten X conducts electricity because its ions become mobile.","img":null},{"t":"X conducts because it contains free electrons.","img":null},{"t":"Its aqueous solution cannot conduct electricity","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv3fsykt8q1m"},{"test":"mv3f9j8jpsmr","n":1791699858053,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"During a science class, a student stated:\n\n“All metals are solid, hard, highly lustrous and good conductors of electricity. All non-metals are dull, brittle and poor conductors of electricity.”\n\nThe teacher explained that although these properties are generally true, there are several important exceptions. For example, mercury is a metal that is liquid at room temperature. Sodium and potassium are metals but are soft enough to be cut with a knife. Most non-metals are dull, but iodine has a lustrous appearance. Similarly, although non-metals usually do not conduct electricity, graphite, a form of carbon, is a good conductor of electricity.\n\nBased on the case study, answer the following questions:\n\nWhich metal is liquid at room temperature?.","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Sodium","img":null},{"t":"Iron","img":null},{"t":"Carbon","img":null},{"t":"Mercury","img":null}],"ans":3,"id":"mv3fu2dh05la"},{"test":"mv4350bp6ct1","n":1791739024690,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Which of the following is a luminous object?","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"stone","img":null},{"t":"glass","img":null},{"t":"moon","img":null},{"t":"sun","img":null}],"ans":3,"id":"mv435jjtdx53"},{"test":"mv4350bp6ct1","n":1791739113803,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"9 o'clock at night is equal to","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"18:00.","img":null},{"t":"9:00","img":null},{"t":"20:00.","img":null},{"t":"21:00","img":null}],"ans":3,"id":"mv437gb2tujg"},{"test":"mv4350bp6ct1","n":1791739397340,"type":"mcq","topic":"","q":"Force does not depend on","qImg":null,"exp":"","expImg":null,"tol":0,"opts":[{"t":"Shape of body","img":null},{"t":"Mass of body","img":null},{"t":"Position of body","img":null},{"t":"Speed of body","img":null}],"ans":1,"id":"mv43dj31fbw1"},{